#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-remote-desktop: Settings › Remote play › "Use this PC from anywhere" (docs/REMOTE-DESKTOP.md). This PC's
desktop (or whatever is on its screen) on another computer or phone with Moonlight, through Tailscale: Sunshine (which
comes with Hearth OS) with Hearth's low-latency settings, reachable only through Tailscale unless you choose your home
network too, never the internet.

Your choices live in ~/.config/nimbus/remote-desktop.json (on, reach, keepAwake), written only when you change one,
through hearth_settings_io (atomic, .bak, merge under a lock; defaults filled in when read, never saved). Off by default.
Not settings, never in that file:
  - Sunshine's login for Hearth: ~/.local/share/nimbus/remote-play.json, 0600 (shared with Settings › Remote play's
    pairing in hearth-core remote.rs); made on this PC the first time, used only on 127.0.0.1, never shown or logged;
  - what Hearth changed in Sunshine's own config, to put it back when you turn this off:
    ~/.local/state/nimbus/remote-desktop.json;
  - who is streaming now and the traffic samples: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hearth-remote-desktop/.

  hearth-remote-desktop status                 JSON: on, reach, Sunshine, the firewall, Tailscale's name and address for
                                               Moonlight, paired devices, who is streaming now (direct or relay), tips
  hearth-remote-desktop set on on|off          turn it on (Sunshine tuned, Tailscale-only rule, starts with your session)
                                               or off (all of that undone; Sunshine stays on if Remote play is on)
  hearth-remote-desktop set reach tailscale|home
  hearth-remote-desktop set keepAwake on|off   stay awake while a device is streaming
  hearth-remote-desktop start                  turn it on again after Sunshine was stopped (what "on" does, saved as is)
  hearth-remote-desktop pin PIN [NAME]         Moonlight's 4 numbers, sent to Sunshine on this PC
  hearth-remote-desktop unpair UUID            that device can't stream anymore (it can pair again)
  hearth-remote-desktop check [IP]             tailscale ping that device (the one streaming when not given)
  hearth-remote-desktop session start|end      Sunshine's prep command (each stream's start and end); always exits 0
  hearth-remote-desktop gate                   Sunshine's ExecStartPre while Tailscale only: waits for the rule
  hearth-remote-desktop awake                  the transient unit that keeps the PC awake while a device streams
  hearth-remote-desktop quick                  who's streaming, in short (Game Mode's Quick Access)
Output: one JSON line; failures print "error: ..." and exit 1. No shell anywhere: every command is an argument list.
"""
